# Vercel serves app/dist, so this list is not about hiding anything from the public —
# only about what the build is allowed to not have.  Every pattern is anchored with a
# leading slash: .vercelignore matches like .gitignore, so a bare "src/" also matched
# app/src/, the app's own source never reached the build, and Rollup failed with
# "could not resolve /src/main.tsx".
#
# /src stays IN the deployment source: the React app imports the trip content from it
# (data.json and routes.json, via the @trip alias).
/legacy/
/.claude/
/CLAUDE.md
/CLAUDE 2.md
